graphene structures can be calculated by using a quantum annealer. This simple system is used to guide the reader    
through the steps needed to translate a chemical structure (a set of atoms) and energy model to a representation that
can be implemented on quantum annealers (a set of qubits). We discuss in detail how different energy contributions   
can be included in the model and what their effect is on the final result. The code used to run the simulation on    
D-Wave quantum annealers is made available as a Jupyter Notebook. This Tutorial was designed to be a quick-start     
guide for the computational chemists interested in running their first quantum annealing simulations.}               
